parseInt(next());\n        }\n\n        long nextLong() {\n            return Long.parseLong(next());\n        }\n\n        double nextDouble() {\n            return Double.parseDouble(next());\n        }\n    }\n\n    public void run() {\n        FastScanner fs = new FastScanner();\n        PrintWriter pw = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n\n        int n = fs.nextInt();\n        int budget = fs.nextInt();\n        int[] arr = new int[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            arr[i] = fs.nextInt();\n        }\n\n        // Precompute prefix sums for odd and even counts\n        int[] oddPrefix = new int[n + 1];\n        int[] evenPrefix = new int[n + 1];\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            oddPrefix[i + 1] = oddPrefix[i] + (arr[i] % 2 == 1 ? 1 : 0);\n            evenPrefix[i + 1] = evenPrefix[i] + (arr[i] % 2 == 0 ? 1 : 0);\n        }\n        \n        // Find all valid cut positions where odd == even in the prefix\n        List<Integer> validCutPositions = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {\n            // Check if prefix [0, i-1] has equal odd and even counts\n            int oddCount = oddPrefix[i];\n            int evenCount = evenPrefix[i];\n            if (oddCount == evenCount) {\n                validCutPositions.add(i);\n            }\n        }\n        \n        // Compute costs between adjacent elements for potential cuts\n        // A cut at position i means between arr[i-1] and arr[i]\n        List<Integer> costs = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (int pos : validCutPositions) {\n            int cost = Math.abs(arr[pos - 1] - arr[pos]);\n            costs.add(cost);\n        }\n        \n        // Now we want to select maximum number of cuts (from valid positions)\n        // such that total cost <= budget\n        // This is a classic greedy knapsack-like problem: select maximum items with minimum total cost\n        Collections.sort(costs);\n        \n        int maxCuts = 0;\n        int totalCost = 0;\n        for (int cost : costs) {\n            if (totalCost + cost <= budget) {\n                totalCost += cost;\n                maxCuts++;\n            } else {\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        pw.println(maxCuts);\n        pw.close();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        new Thread(null, new Main(), \"Main\", 1 << 26).start();\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-3.576278118089249e-07, -4.851700214203447e-05, -2.50339189733495e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.2291887944447808e-05, -2.8609820219571702e-05, -2.264974000354414e-06, -8.22540732769994e-06, -7.855583680793643e-05, -5.602820692729438e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.02058090642094612, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -1.0847986231965479e-05, -0.0007179781678132713, -0.0021941415034234524, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.07287787614041e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.00029404606902971864, -0.01815616525709629, -2.622600959512056e-06, -1.4662635294371285e-05, -2.145764938177308e-06, -0.00015090756642166525, -0.0001456631434848532, -2.0146166207268834e-05, -8.344646857949556e-07, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -0.00017987063620239496, -2.1457441107486375e-05, -3.5523738915799186e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.2186455882765586e-06, -1.8596476365928538e-05, -6.198863957251888e-06, -2.7179348762729205e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.098061486321967e-05, -8.821448318485636e-06, -1.7762025890988298e-05, -3.3378546504536644e-06, -3.814689989667386e-06, -4.0531076592742465e-06, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -1.8954096958623268e-05, -8.344646857949556e-07, -3.933898824470816e-06, -5.602820692729438e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -9.536738616588991e-07, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -7.390703103737906e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, -9.536738616588991e-07, -2.610649426060263e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -7.152555099310121e-07, -3.933898824470816e-06, -7.867782187531702e-06, -1.1920858014491387e-